---
const questions = [
  {
    question: "Is the free tier really free?",
    answer:
      "Virtual Labs is paid in LAB Coin, which 8Labs grants free while it is available. You can run one lab of each size at a time. If you run out of coins, open a support ticket.",
    href: "https://my.8labs.id/products/virtual-labs",
    label: "See Virtual Labs plans",
  },
  {
    question: "Which operating systems can I run?",
    answer:
      "Debian, Ubuntu, CentOS, Rocky Linux, AlmaLinux, and FreeBSD, all on KVM with full root access. Anything that runs on Linux will run. For anything else, ask in the Telegram community before you order.",
    href: "https://t.me/virtual_8labs",
    label: "Ask the community",
  },
  {
    question: "How do I pay, and when does billing stop?",
    answer:
      "Top up a rupiah balance by QRIS, bank virtual account, or crypto. Plans run for a day, three days, a week, or a month. Rupiah plans renew from your balance automatically, so cancel in Client Panel to stop them: shutting down or deleting the VM is not enough. LAB Coin plans never renew on their own.",
    href: "/docs/billing-plans/overview/",
    label: "Understand billing and cancellation",
  },
  {
    question: "How long until I can use my server?",
    answer:
      "Usually under two minutes after payment. Wait for the installation status to finish, not just a Running label. If setup fails, contact support before you reorder.",
    href: "/docs/getting-started/intro/#wait-for-provisioning",
    label: "Follow the first-access guide",
  },
  {
    question: "Are backups included?",
    answer:
      "No. VDL and ElasticLabs plans include two snapshots, but they are stored on the same server as your VM. If that server fails, both are gone. Keep your own copy of anything important, and test that you can restore it.",
    href: "/docs/servers/backups/",
    label: "Review recovery options",
  },
];
---

<div>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <div>
      <h2 id="purchase-questions-heading" class="section-title">
        Questions before you start
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-8 min-w-0 border-t border-grid">
      {
        questions.map((item) => (
          <details class="faq border-b border-grid">
            <summary class="flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 text-base font-medium leading-relaxed text-line transition-colors duration-150 hover:text-red-ink">
              {item.question}
              <svg
                class="faq-mark h-4 w-4 shrink-0"
                viewBox="0 0 16 16"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.5"
                aria-hidden="true">
                <>
                  <path d="M2 8h12" />
                  <path class="faq-mark-v" d="M8 2v12" />
                </>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="max-w-prose pb-6 pr-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-cool">
              <p>{item.answer}</p>
              <a
                href={item.href}
                class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-[2.75rem] items-center font-medium text-red-ink underline underline-offset-4">
                {item.label}
              </a>
            </div>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .faq summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .faq-mark-v {
    transform-origin: center;
    transition: transform 200ms cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1);
  }
  .faq[open] .faq-mark-v {
    transform: scaleY(0);
  }
  /* Progressive enhancement: animate the answer's height where supported. */
  @supports (interpolate-size: allow-keywords) {
    .faq {
      interpolate-size: allow-keywords;
    }
    .faq::details-content {
      block-size: 0;
      overflow: clip;
      transition:
        block-size 160ms cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1),
        content-visibility 160ms allow-discrete;
    }
    .faq[open]::details-content {
      block-size: auto;
      transition-duration: 220ms;
    }
  }
</style>
